meta {
  name: Revert Payment
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/revert
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "Reverted from Payments ledger"
  }
}

docs {
  Revert a SINGLE order payment (the Finance → Payments "Revert" action) — not the
  whole order. The row is kept ACTIVE but its money fields are zeroed and its
  original amount preserved in `revertedAmount` (its `netAmount` snapshot is kept so
  the order's net total — summed across payment rows — survives). The order's paid
  amount, `paymentStatus`, `billStatus` and the Outstanding report then recompute off
  the remaining non-reverted money, while the reverted row stays visible in the
  ledger's "Reverted" tab. The order and its total are left untouched.

  Permission `finance:payments__cancel_direct_order_payment`. Guarded like Delete
  Payment (403 `PAYMENT_COLLECTION_BY_OTHER_USER_NOT_ALLOWED`). Blocked with 409
  `PAYMENT_REVERT_BLOCKED_ORDER_INVOICED` when the order has been consolidated into
  an invoice (revert the invoice receipt instead). `reason` is optional.
}
